          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=UTF-8",
            "text": "{\"hits\":[{\"id\":2048027,\"kind\":\"regular\",\"category\":\"charity\",\"subcategory\":\"international_aid\",\"type\":\"screening\",\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"state\":\"published\",\"venue_type\":null,\"organization_id\":58,\"billetto_score\":null,\"name\":\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen | Film screening and conversation with Aziz Hathaleen\",\"name_truncated\":\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen | Film…\",\"description\":\"Join the Britain Palestine Project for a public screening of Palestinian human rights organisation Al-Haq’s investigative film The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen: Beyond a Settler Crime , followed by a conversation with Awdah’s brother, Aziz Hathaleen and Zainah Haroun from Al-Haq. Awdah was a Palestinian teacher, father of three and human rights defender who contributed to the Oscar-winning documentary No Other Land . On 28 July 2025, he was shot and killed while filming a settler attack in his village of Umm al-Kheir, in Masafer Yatta in the occupied West Bank. Using video footage and a reconstruction of the scene, Al-Haq’s film examines the circumstances of Awdah’s killing and places it in the wider context of settler violence in the West Bank. After the screening, we’ll hear from Aziz about his brother and what life is like for the community of Umm al-Kheir today. Tickets are free and everyone is welcome. Please reserve your place through Billetto. Guests will be invited to make an optional donation on the night to support the community of Umm al-Kheir.\",\"price\":0.0,\"price_range\":\"Free\",\"image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/19buhzpa39j6xs71uw8zmrfdvio8?w=640&h=360&fit=crop&auto=compress%2Cformat&rect=0%2C50%2C960%2C540&s=90a0cfd3c971d789c7a542881fbaf026\",\"uses_generic_billetto_image\":false,\"keywords\":[],\"organizer_id\":4427429,\"organizer_image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/b0q9lcgh3cx4ulsizctshfxfl8rh?s=2272ad4ae78a4c31a6584444c77c171b\",\"url\":\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/the-killing-of-awdah-hathaleen-film-screen